Description: turns Ubuntu into a rig for playing music live
 Installing this package sets a stock Ubuntu desktop up for low-latency
 audio and brings in what a live rig needs:
 .
  * kernel options for low latency (full preemption, threaded interrupts),
    the same ones Ubuntu Studio boots with;
  * realtime priority and locked memory for everyone who logs in;
  * PipeWire at one fixed rate, as the JACK server for every JACK program,
    with sound devices that are never put to sleep;
  * no USB autosuspend, low swappiness, the ntsync driver for Wine;
  * a desktop that does not blank, sleep, index files or update by itself;
  * the StageRig look: wallpaper, dark style, boot and login screens;
  * StageRig, a set of free instruments and effects, and General MIDI
    soundfonts; VST Environment (Windows plugins) for each user at first login.
 .
 stagerig-os-check reports what is in order and what is not. Purging the
 package (apt purge) undoes its settings.
